# Local install state: passwords, build log, backups. Never commit.
.env
# A copy of .env carries the same real passwords. `.env` alone did not cover
# the ones the 2026-11-24 incident left behind, so one `git add -A` would have
# committed them (rule A2). .env.example stays tracked: it holds no secret.
.env.bak*
.env.sav*
.env.old*
build.log
backups/
